<title>GERMANY: Schmalbach shareholders agree joint-venture plans.</title>
<headline>Schmalbach shareholders agree joint-venture plans.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>German packaging producer Schmalbach-Lubeca said on Tuesday that its shareholders had approved an earlier agreed deal to sell its metal packaging activities to a joint-venture Impress Metal Packaging Holding B.V. Amsterdam.</p>
<p>In the deal Schmalbach and its partner French metals group Pechiney SA will each hold a 20 percent stake in the new company.</p>
<p>UK group Doughty Hanson &amp; Co and the management of Impress Packaging Holding B.V. will have a 60 percent stake.</p>
<p>The merged business will have turnover above seven billion francs from 35 factories spread across 12 countries, it said.</p>
<p>Schmalbach-Lubeca is a subsidiary of German industrial group Viag AG.</p>
<p>The merged company will have 7,850 staff.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
